on-arrival: {!
// the party grows month by month in 1919; between the great clashes the state of siege eases
Q.repression -= 6; Q.militancy -= 2;
if (!Q.ultraleft_gone && Q.heidelberg_outcome == 0) { Q.ultraleft_satisfaction = Math.max(Q.ultraleft_satisfaction, 30); }
var g = Math.max(1.05, Math.min(1.35, 1.24 + Q.worker_support / 200 - Q.repression / 400));
for (var d of Q.districts) { Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= g; }
RG.news('Communist Zentrale drafts theses on elections and the unions', 2);
!}

= The Theses

The second party congress is called for October, in secret, somewhere in Baden. [+ party_chair +] has drafted theses: the party must use elections as a platform, work inside the trade unions and be one centralised party, not a federation of districts. The last thesis says that whoever rejects these principles stands outside the party.

The Left Radicals know the last thesis is about them. They hold Hamburg, Bremen and much of Berlin, and they say a congress elected by the members would vote the theses down. The Zentrale must decide how the delegates are chosen.

- @zentrale: The Zentrale draws up the mandates.
- @districts: One delegation per district, whatever its size.
- @free: Free elections, so many delegates for so many members.

@zentrale
subtitle: A congress the Zentrale can rely on. The Left Radicals will call it packed before it meets.
on-arrival: heid_mandates = 1; unity -= 5; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 10; lean_luxemburgist += 2

@districts
subtitle: Thuringia and Halle will count as much as Hamburg. Everyone will know why.
on-arrival: heid_mandates = 2; unity -= 2; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 5; lean_unionist += 1

@free
subtitle: Party democracy, as Luxemburg wanted it. The Left Radicals may well win.
on-arrival: heid_mandates = 0; unity += 4; ultraleft_satisfaction += 6

The districts elect their delegates in crowded, angry meetings.
